 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R13 (block 261000) -- LAND ACQUISITION: the three modes by which a plot changes hands, all graph-native. bl_buy (seller-priced MARKET, transfers coin + moves the `owns` edge, Sigma conserved) + bl_buy_fail (the CAN'T-AFFORD control: coin<price -> no transfer). bl_claim (HOMESTEAD unowned FRONTIER land, first-come via the owned==0 guard: a second claimant to the same plot no longer matches). bl_grant (COUNCIL grant, R9: the council holds a plot + a `granted_to` edge -> `owns` moves council->recipient). LAND is FINITE / NON-PRODUCED / CONSERVED: NO rule mints or destroys a Plot node (no add_node/del_node); every mode only MOVES or ADDS an `owns` edge over a fixed set of pre-existing Plot nodes. The structural-exclusion control is ABSENCE: all-owned + no-seller + no-grant -> nothing matches -> the landless acquire nothing by wanting. Composes existing DSL Terms; ZERO new Rust.",
